CYD_EMU
=======

CYD_EMU is a fork of esp32sim, https://github.com/mikroverk/esp32sim, an ESP32 emulator by
Joakim Eriksson (@joakimeriksson), Alice (@aliceisjustplaying) and Mattia Fiumara (@mfiumara)
and its contributors. It is maintained separately and is not affiliated with, or endorsed by,
the esp32sim authors or Espressif Systems.

- The repository root is esp32sim with this fork's changes (branch cyd-2432s028r upstream of
  this repository): the Cheap Yellow Display boards and the features cyd-lab uses. Its full
  history, including all upstream commits and authors, is kept. It is licensed under the MIT
  licence in LICENSE, copyright (c) 2026 the esp32sim authors named there.
- cyd-lab/ is the desktop workbench by Gareth Johnstone, licensed under the MIT licence in
  cyd-lab/LICENSE, copyright (c) 2026 Gareth Johnstone.
- esp32sim's original README is the second part of README.md, below CYD_EMU's section.

Third-party code, data and firmware keep their own licences. esp32sim's list is at the end of
README.md; cyd-lab's (firmware catalogue, ESPHome images and the crates in the
Windows build) is cyd-lab/packaging/NOTICE.txt, which the release zip ships in LICENSES/ together
with generated third-party crate lists.

The two ESPHome example images in cyd-lab/assets/firmware/ (esphome-ha-cyd-2432s028r*.factory.bin,
built into cyd-lab.exe) are GPL-3.0 binaries: they contain ESPHome's runtime
(https://github.com/esphome/esphome, 2026.10.0, GPL-3.0) together with ESP-IDF (Apache-2.0) and
LVGL (MIT). Their corresponding source is ESPHome 2026.10.0 plus the configs in
cyd-lab/firmware/esphome-ha/ (MIT); cyd-lab/tools/build_esphome_ha.py rebuilds them. The GPL-3.0
applies to those images only, not to the rest of this repository. Mask ROM ELFs (espressif/esp-rom-elfs,
Apache-2.0) are downloaded at first run or by tools/fetch-rom-elfs.sh, never committed.
